id: lending
name: Lending and loan origination
industry: Banking & financial services
domain: Retail and agricultural lending - from enquiry to disbursement and repayment
scope: Applicants and co-applicants, dealers and sourcing channels, loan products and schemes, applications, credit assessment and underwriting, sanction, collateral and financed assets, disbursement, repayment schedule and collections status.
summary: Describes how a lender originates and services a loan: who applies and through which channel, what is financed, how the application is assessed and sanctioned, how money is disbursed and how it is repaid. It is a starter model for banks and NBFCs financing vehicles, tractors, equipment or personal needs.
purpose: A shared vocabulary for loan origination, underwriting and portfolio analytics; the target model when integrating the loan origination system, the core lending system and the collections system.
read: Start from Loan application. It is made by an Applicant (with optional Co-applicants and Guarantors), sourced through a Dealer or Branch, for a Loan product, to finance an Asset. A Credit assessment with Bureau reports and Underwriting decisions leads to a Sanction. A Loan account is opened against the sanction; Disbursements pay it out, a Repayment schedule of Instalments defines what is due, and Payments settle them.
in: Parties and their roles; Products, schemes and pricing; Application, assessment and sanction; Assets and collateral; Disbursement and repayment
out: Treasury and funding; General ledger accounting; Legal recovery proceedings; Deposit products
std: fibo | high | Concepts for loans, borrowers, lenders, collateral and interest follow FIBO's Loans and Business Entities domains. | Loan, Borrower, Lender, Collateral, InterestRate, LegalEntity
std: mismo | medium | The application - underwriting - closing - servicing lifecycle follows the MISMO reference model. | Loan, Borrower, Underwriting, Closing, Servicing, CreditReport
std: schema | medium | People, organisations and addresses are aligned to schema.org for exchange. | schema:Person, schema:Organization, schema:PostalAddress
std: iso20022 | low | Payment and disbursement instructions follow ISO 20022 payment concepts. | PaymentInstruction, CashAccount
== Party | Parties and roles | The people and organisations involved in a loan and the roles they play.
Party | A person or organisation that takes part in a lending relationship.
  - name : string !
  - mobile number : string
  - email : string
  > has address > Address *
  > has identity document > IdentityDocument *
Individual : Party | A natural person. | =schema:Person
  - date of birth : date
  - gender : string
  - occupation : string
  - annual income : decimal | Declared or assessed yearly income.
Organization : Party | A company, firm or other body acting as one party. | =schema:Organization
  - registration number : string
  - date of incorporation : date
Applicant : Party | The party that applies for the loan and is primarily liable to repay it. Also called the borrower once the loan is sanctioned.
  - customer id : string !
  - existing customer : boolean
CoApplicant : Party | A party that applies jointly and shares liability for repayment.
  - relationship to applicant : string
Guarantor : Party | A party that undertakes to repay if the borrower does not.
Dealer : Organization | A seller of the financed asset who sources applications for the lender.
  - dealer code : string !
  - empanelled on : date
  - active : boolean
Branch : Organization | An office of the lender that sources, processes or services loans.
  - branch code : string !
  - region : string
  - state : string
Employee | A member of the lender's staff acting on applications.
  - employee id : string !
  - designation : string
  > works at > Branch 1
Address | A postal location of a party or an asset. | =schema:PostalAddress
  - line : string
  - village or city : string
  - district : string
  - state : string
  - postal code : string
IdentityDocument | An official document proving a party's identity or address (KYC).
  - document number : string !
  - verified : boolean
  > of type > IdentityDocumentType 1
IdentityDocumentType | The kind of identity document.
  * Aadhaar, PAN, Passport, Voter ID, Driving licence
== Product | Products and pricing | What the lender offers and on what terms.
LoanProduct | A type of loan the lender offers, with its eligibility and pricing rules.
  - product code : string !
  - product name : string !
  - minimum amount : decimal
  - maximum amount : decimal
  - maximum tenure months : integer
  > in category > ProductCategory 1
ProductCategory | A grouping of loan products.
  * Tractor loan, Vehicle loan, Equipment loan, Personal loan, Business loan, Gold loan
Scheme | A time-bound variant of a product with special rates or terms, often tied to a manufacturer or season.
  - scheme code : string !
  - valid from : date
  - valid to : date
  > applies to > LoanProduct 1
InterestRate | The price of the loan expressed as a yearly percentage.
  - annual rate percent : decimal !
  > of type > RateType 1
RateType | Whether the rate is fixed for the term or follows a benchmark.
  * Fixed, Floating
Charge | A fee levied on the loan in addition to interest.
  - amount : decimal !
  > of type > ChargeType 1
ChargeType | The kind of fee.
  * Processing fee, Documentation charge, Insurance premium, Stamp duty, Late payment charge
== Origination | Application and underwriting | From the first enquiry to the lender's decision.
LoanApplication | A request for a loan of a stated amount and tenure, moving through the lender's process.
  - application number : string !
  - applied on : date !
  - requested amount : decimal !
  - requested tenure months : integer
  - purpose : string
  > made by > Applicant 1 | The primary applicant. | applies for
  > has co-applicant > CoApplicant *
  > guaranteed by > Guarantor *
  > for product > LoanProduct 1
  > under scheme > Scheme ?
  > sourced by > Dealer ? | The dealer who brought the application. | sourced
  > logged at > Branch 1
  > to finance > Asset ?
  > has status > ApplicationStatus 1
  > handled by > Employee *
ApplicationStatus | The stage an application has reached.
  * Lead, Logged in, Under assessment, Sanctioned, Rejected, Withdrawn, Disbursed
CreditAssessment | The lender's evaluation of the applicant's ability and willingness to repay.
  - assessed on : date !
  - assessed income : decimal
  - obligations per month : decimal
  - foir percent : decimal | Fixed obligations to income ratio.
  - ltv percent : decimal | Loan amount as a share of the asset's value.
  - internal score : decimal
  > assesses > LoanApplication 1 | | assessed by
  > uses > BureauReport *
  > performed by > Employee ?
BureauReport | A credit history report on a party obtained from a credit bureau.
  - bureau name : string !
  - score : integer
  - pulled on : date !
  - active loans : integer
  - overdue amount : decimal
  > about > Party 1
FieldVerification | A physical check of the applicant's residence, business or land.
  - visited on : date
  - outcome : string
  - remarks : string
  > verifies > LoanApplication 1
UnderwritingDecision | The lender's formal decision on an application, with any conditions.
  - decided on : date !
  - conditions : string
  > decides > LoanApplication 1
  > has outcome > DecisionOutcome 1
  > decided by > Employee 1
  > has reason > RejectionReason *
DecisionOutcome | The result of underwriting.
  * Approve, Approve with conditions, Refer, Reject
RejectionReason | Why an application was declined.
  * Low bureau score, Insufficient income, High existing obligations, Negative field report, Policy deviation, Incomplete documents
Deviation | An approved exception to credit policy on a specific application.
  - policy parameter : string !
  - justification : string
  > on > LoanApplication 1
  > approved by > Employee 1
Sanction | The lender's commitment to lend a stated amount on stated terms, valid for a period.
  - sanction number : string !
  - sanctioned on : date !
  - sanctioned amount : decimal !
  - tenure months : integer !
  - valid until : date
  > sanctions > LoanApplication 1 | | sanctioned as
  > at rate > InterestRate 1
  > with charge > Charge *
== Security | Assets and collateral | What is financed and what secures the loan.
Asset | A thing financed by the loan, such as a tractor, vehicle or machine.
  - make : string
  - model : string
  - variant : string
  - engine or serial number : string
  - registration number : string
  - invoice value : decimal
  - on road price : decimal
  > of type > AssetType 1
  > supplied by > Dealer ?
AssetType | The kind of financed asset.
  * Tractor, Implement, Harvester, Commercial vehicle, Car, Two-wheeler, Machinery
Collateral | Property pledged to the lender that may be taken if the loan is not repaid.
  - description : string
  - assessed value : decimal
  - valued on : date
  > secures > LoanAccount 1 | | secured by
  > is asset > Asset ?
  > of type > CollateralType 1
CollateralType | The kind of security.
  * Hypothecation of asset, Mortgage of land, Gold, Fixed deposit lien, Personal guarantee
Insurance | Cover on the financed asset or the borrower's life, assigned to the lender.
  - policy number : string !
  - insurer : string
  - sum insured : decimal
  - expires on : date
  > covers > Asset ?
== Servicing | Disbursement and repayment | Paying the loan out and getting it back.
LoanAccount | The loan as booked after sanction: the running record of what was lent, what is due and what was paid.
  - loan account number : string !
  - opened on : date !
  - principal outstanding : decimal
  - days past due : integer
  - closed on : date
  > booked from > Sanction 1
  > owed by > Applicant 1 | | owes
  > serviced at > Branch 1
  > has status > LoanStatus 1
  > has schedule > RepaymentSchedule 1
LoanStatus | The servicing state of a loan account.
  * Active, Overdue, Non-performing, Closed, Foreclosed, Written off
Disbursement | A payment of loan money by the lender, in full or in a tranche.
  - disbursed on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  - reference number : string
  > against > LoanAccount 1 | | paid out through
  > paid to > Party 1 | The dealer or borrower who receives the money.
  > by mode > PaymentMode 1
RepaymentSchedule | The plan of instalments agreed for a loan account.
  - instalment count : integer !
  - first due date : date
  > has frequency > RepaymentFrequency 1
  > has instalment > Instalment +
RepaymentFrequency | How often instalments fall due.
  * Monthly, Quarterly, Half-yearly, Yearly
Instalment | One scheduled amount due on a date, made of principal and interest.
  - sequence : integer !
  - due date : date !
  - principal due : decimal
  - interest due : decimal
  - paid : boolean
Payment | Money received from the borrower against a loan account.
  - received on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  - bounced : boolean
  > credited to > LoanAccount 1
  > settles > Instalment *
  > by mode > PaymentMode 1
PaymentMode | How money is paid.
  * NACH mandate, UPI, Cheque, Cash, Bank transfer
rule: constraint | Disbursement needs sanction | A disbursement can only be made against a loan account booked from a valid, unexpired sanction. | Disbursement, Sanction
rule: constraint | Disbursed within sanction | The total disbursed on a loan account cannot exceed the sanctioned amount. | Disbursement, Sanction
rule: derivation | Loan to value | LTV percent is the sanctioned amount divided by the asset's on-road price or assessed value. | CreditAssessment, Asset
rule: derivation | Days past due | Days past due is counted from the due date of the oldest unpaid instalment. | LoanAccount, Instalment
rule: constraint | Rejection needs a reason | An underwriting decision with outcome Reject must carry at least one rejection reason. | UnderwritingDecision
rule: disjoint | Person or organisation | A party is either an individual or an organisation, never both. | Individual, Organization
uc: Dealer rejection rate | Sales head | Which dealers have the highest share of applications rejected at underwriting, and for which reasons? | LoanApplication, Dealer, UnderwritingDecision, DecisionOutcome, RejectionReason | sourced by, decides, has outcome, UnderwritingDecision.has reason
uc: Sanction to disbursement ageing | Operations manager | Which sanctions have not been disbursed within 30 days? | Sanction, LoanAccount, Disbursement | Sanction.sanctioned on, booked from, against, Disbursement.disbursed on
uc: Portfolio at risk by product and branch | Risk manager | What share of outstanding principal is more than 90 days past due, by product and branch? | LoanAccount, Sanction, LoanApplication, LoanProduct, Branch | LoanAccount.days past due, LoanAccount.principal outstanding, booked from, sanctions, for product, serviced at
uc: Bureau score versus delinquency | Credit policy analyst | How does the bureau score at application relate to later overdue status? | BureauReport, CreditAssessment, LoanApplication, Sanction, LoanAccount, LoanStatus | BureauReport.score, uses, assesses, sanctions, booked from, LoanAccount.has status
